   "id": 616301,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In what proved to be his final Annual Message to Congress, President Franklin Roosevelt said, “After the last war, we gave up the hope of achieving a better peace because we had not the courage to fulfill our responsibilities in an admittedly imperfect world. We must not let that happen again.” In this quote, Roosevelt was referring to the failure of",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1173171,
     "content_html": "the policy of appeasement"
    },
    {
     "id": 1173170,
     "content_html": "America and its European allies in allowing dictatorships to arise in Europe"
    },
    {
     "id": 1173169,
     "content_html": "the Washington Naval Conference agreements"
    },
    {
     "id": 1173172,
     "content_html": "the United States to join the League of Nations"
    }
   ],
